  },
  "question": {
    "text": "If the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math> is differentiable on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "15",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>Also given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is differentiable on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math></p><p>So, finding LHD and RHD at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, for function to be continuous at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>48</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p>"
  }
}